<p>Keep one in your bag. Keep one at work. Give one to somebody whose phone is somehow always at 11%. Put them wherever they’re most likely to be available when the tiny battery-powered master key to your entire life starts begging for electricity.</p>
<p>Because we’ve made your phone responsible for an unreasonable percentage of your ability to participate in society.</p>
<p>Might as well keep the damn thing alive.</p>